2 L 171.42313 50.744802 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p26abb9d098)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 283.747805 138.336 L 373.607545 138.336 L 373.607545 16.896 L 283.747805 16.896 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p26abb9d098)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 43.373 138.336 L 43.373 10.824 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_7\"><path d=\"M 43.373 138.336 L 389.333 138.336 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(96.01645 116.474406) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\" transform=\"translate(136.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(207.504875 48.776802) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" d=\"M 3482 4749 Q 3546 4749 3565 4729 Q 3584 4710 3578 4653 L 3552 4307 Q 3546 4262 3536 4249 Q 3526 4237 3462 4237 L 1286 4237 Q 1210 4237 1210 4166 L 1094 2778 Q 1088 2733 1113 2710 Q 1139 2688 1171 2701 Q 1408 2822 1648 2915 Q 1888 3008 2234 3008 Q 2656 3008 3021 2854 Q 3386 2701 3606 2381 Q 3827 2061 3827 1555 Q 3827 1043 3593 681 Q 3360 320 2947 128 Q 2534 -64 2003 -64 Q 1517 -64 1085 105 Q 653 275 352 602 Q 326 640 323 669 Q 320 698 365 730 L 640 954 Q 691 992 749 934 Q 922 774 1088 652 Q 1254 531 1456 464 Q 1658 397 1926 397 Q 2342 397 2630 544 Q 2918 691 3072 950 Q 3226 1210 3226 1536 Q 3226 1882 3078 2102 Q 2931 2323 2684 2432 Q 2438 2541 2138 2541 Q 1798 2541 1529 2419 Q 1261 2298 1037 2163 Q 986 2138 973 2144 Q 960 2150 922 2170 L 608 2349 Q 550 2381 553 2397 Q 557 2413 563 2490 L 736 4659 Q 742 4717 764 4733 Q 787 4749 877 4749 L 3482 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(155.109375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(320.021425 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" d=\"M 3456 4749 Q 3507 4749 3532 4723 Q 3558 4698 3552 4672 L 3546 4442 Q 3546 4390 3520 4329 Q 3494 4269 3456 4211 Q 3200 3827 2960 3385 Q 2720 2944 2515 2477 Q 2310 2010 2147 1571 Q 1984 1133 1875 758 Q 1766 384 1728 122 Q 1715 0 1632 0 L 1126 0 Q 1024 0 1050 109 Q 1139 467 1289 918 Q 1440 1370 1661 1891 Q 1882 2413 2182 2982 Q 2483 3552 2861 4147 Q 2886 4186 2880 4211 Q 2874 4237 2816 4237 L 339 4237 Q 262 4237 262 4314 L 307 4685 Q 314 4749 403 4749 L 3456 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(149.609375 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p26abb9d098\"><rect x=\"43.373\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Operating profit by year ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Profit = (members × $95 × 12 + $0.45M) × 95% − $0.95M.</p> <ul><li>Year 1: 600 members → <b>$0.13M</b></li><li>Year 2: 1,000 members → <b>$0.56M</b></li><li>Year 3: 1,200 members → <b>$0.78M</b></li></ul> <p>Cumulative after three years: $1.46M of the $2.2M. At year-three profit, the remaining $0.74M takes another 0.9 years: payback ≈ <b>3.9 years</b>, inside the five-year hurdle.</p>"},{"q":"Members climb 2.2 times a week; 40% of visits are in the weekday 6-9pm peak (15 hours a week); a session lasts 2 hours. How many people are in the gym at peak with 1,200 members? (Assume day-pass visitors climb mostly at weekends and off-peak, so ignore them for the evening peak.)","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Peak arrivals per hour: 1,200 × 2.2 × 40% ÷ 15 = 70.4.</p> <p>Each stays 2 hours, so about <b>141 people</b> are climbing at once, against a safe limit of 120.</p> <p>Maximum members before peak overcrowding: 1,200 × 120 ÷ 141 ≈ <b>1,023</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the plan's year-three membership doesn't physically fit. Unless peak demand is shifted, membership caps at about 1,023.</p>","note":"This is the crux of the case. Strong candidates spot the capacity question before being asked."},{"q":"What does the cap do to the investment case?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>At about 1,023 members, steady-state profit is $0.59M instead of $0.78M. Payback stretches: after year two the remaining $1.51M takes 2.6 more years: about <b>4.6 years</b>, still inside five, but with little margin.</p> <p><b>Fixes:</b> off-peak memberships at a lower price (students, shift workers, parents), corporate memberships used at lunchtime, timed booking at peak, and a higher peak-access price.</p>"},{"q":"What would you recommend to the investors?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Go ahead, but redesign the membership model before opening: an off-peak tier priced ~30% lower, a peak tier priced higher, and pre-sold corporate memberships for daytime use. Track peak occupancy from day one.</p>"}],"reco":"Go ahead, with a different membership model. On the plan's numbers the gym pays back in about 3.9 years, but at 1,200 members about 141 people would be climbing at peak against a safe limit of 120, so membership effectively caps at about 1,023 and payback stretches to about 4.6 years. I recommend launching with peak and off-peak tiers and pre-selling daytime corporate memberships to grow beyond the cap. Risk: if off-peak demand is weak, payback lands close to the hurdle. Next step: survey local climbers on when they would visit and at what price.","great":["Models the ramp-up instead of using steady state from day one","Checks physical capacity at peak","Converts the capacity limit into a membership cap","Fixes the problem with pricing tiers, not just 'more marketing'"],"id":34,"slug":"orbit-climbing"}